{"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StateManagement","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ThemingGuide","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/FocusSystem","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StatusBarGuide","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/AppearanceAndColors","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/CustomViews","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/KeyboardShortcuts","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/PaletteReference","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ListAndTable","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/LayoutSystem"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Guides","title":"Guides"}],"metadata":{"role":"collectionGroup","modules":[{"name":"TUIkit"}],"title":"Preferences"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tuikit\/preferences"]}],"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Pass data from child views up to their ancestors."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Preferences"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"TUIkit’s preference system enables "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"bottom-up data flow"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the reverse of environment values. While the environment passes data down from parent to child, preferences let child views publish values that ancestors can observe and react to."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The system mirrors SwiftUI’s preference API and consists of three parts:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PreferenceKey"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Protocol that defines a named value type with a default and a reduce strategy"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PreferenceValues"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Type-safe storage that holds all preference values for a scope"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"PreferenceStorage","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Stack-based collector that manages preference contexts per render pass","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A built-in example is ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/NavigationTitleKey","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":": a child view sets ","type":"text"},{"code":".navigationTitle(\"Settings\")","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and the enclosing navigation container reads that preference to render the title bar.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Defining-a-Preference-Key","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Defining a Preference Key"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A preference key declares what type of value it carries and how multiple values from sibling children are combined:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct CounterKey: PreferenceKey {","    static let defaultValue: Int = 0","","    static func reduce(value: inout Int, nextValue: () -> Int) {","        value += nextValue()","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"defaultValue","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"text":": Returned when no child has set this preference","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce(value:nextValue:)"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Combines values when multiple children set the same key"}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The default ","type":"text"},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" implementation simply takes the last value. Override it when you need additive behavior (summing counts), array collection, or other merge strategies.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Setting-a-Preference","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Setting a Preference"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Child views publish a preference using the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".preference(key:value:)"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct ItemView: View {","    var body: some View {","        Text(\"Item\")","            .preference(key: CounterKey.self, value: 1)","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Under the hood, this wraps the view in a ","type":"text"},{"code":"PreferenceModifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that calls ","type":"text"},{"code":"preferences.setValue(_:forKey:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" during rendering. The value is reduced into the current scope using the key’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" function.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Observing-Preferences","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Observing Preferences"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ancestor views react to collected preferences using "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".onPreferenceChange(_:perform:)"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct ItemList: View {","    var body: some View {","        VStack {","            ItemView()","            ItemView()","            ItemView()","        }","        .onPreferenceChange(CounterKey.self) { totalCount in","            \/\/ totalCount == 3 (three children each set value: 1, additive reduce)","        }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The modifier pushes a new preference context, renders all children (which set their preferences), pops the context, and fires the callback with the accumulated result.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"The-Navigation-Title-Shortcut","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The Navigation Title Shortcut"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"TUIkit provides ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/NavigationTitleKey","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" as a built-in preference key with a convenience modifier:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct SettingsPage: View {","    var body: some View {","        VStack {","            Text(\"App settings go here\")","        }","        .navigationTitle(\"Settings\")","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"NavigationTitleKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" uses the default ","type":"text"},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (last value wins), so the deepest child’s title takes precedence.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"How-Preferences-Flow-per-Frame","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"How Preferences Flow per Frame"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Preferences are collected fresh every frame. Here’s the lifecycle within a single render pass:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Reset","type":"text"}]},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"code":"RenderLoop.render()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" calls ","type":"text"},{"code":"preferences.beginRenderPass()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", clearing all callbacks and resetting the stack to a single empty context","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Set"}]},{"type":"text","text":": As the view tree renders top-down, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PreferenceModifier"},{"type":"text","text":" views call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"setValue(_:forKey:)"},{"type":"text","text":", which reduces values into the current stack frame"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Scope"}]},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"code":"OnPreferenceChangeModifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" pushes a new context before rendering its subtree, isolating child preferences"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Collect"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": After the subtree finishes, the modifier pops the context (merging into the parent) and fires the callback with the scoped result"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Discard","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": At the start of the next frame, everything resets: stale preferences never persist"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This per-frame reset ensures preferences always reflect the current view tree. Removed views stop contributing automatically."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Reduce-Strategies","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Reduce Strategies"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":" function determines how multiple children’s values combine. Common patterns:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Strategy"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Implementation"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use Case"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Last value wins","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"value = nextValue()"},{"type":"text","text":" (default)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Titles, labels: deepest child wins","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Additive"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"value += nextValue()","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Counting items, summing heights","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Array collection","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"value.append(contentsOf: nextValue())"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Gathering menu items, breadcrumbs"}]}]]],"header":"row","type":"table"},{"code":["\/\/ Array collection example","struct BreadcrumbKey: PreferenceKey {","    static let defaultValue: [String] = []","","    static func reduce(value: inout [String], nextValue: () -> [String]) {","        value.append(contentsOf: nextValue())","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}]}],"references":{"doc://TUIkit/documentation/TUIkit/ThemingGuide":{"role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Customize the visual appearance of your TUIkit application with palettes."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ThemingGuide","title":"Theming Guide","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/tuikit\/themingguide","kind":"article"},"doc://TUIkit/documentation/TUIkit/NavigationTitleKey":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"NavigationTitleKey","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/tuikit\/navigationtitlekey","title":"NavigationTitleKey","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"NavigationTitleKey","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/NavigationTitleKey","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A preference key for the navigation title."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://TUIkit/documentation/TUIkit/PaletteReference":{"role":"collectionGroup","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/PaletteReference","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A visual reference for all built-in color palettes with their exact color values.","type":"text"